  "title": "Iran and U.S. Reopening Hormuz Strait Amid Global Security Tensions",
  "summary": "Iran’s president denies threatening to resign during talks over the Strait of Hormuz, while the U.S. and Qatar report progress on a ceasefire and the reopening of the strait, though shipping remains blocked.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Iran’s president, Masoud Pezeshkian, denies threatening to resign during talks over the Strait of Hormuz.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The U.S. and Qatar have reported progress on a ceasefire and the reopening of the strait, though shipping remains closed.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both sides have put pressure on Oman to accept a temporary agreement that officials fear will leave Iran retaining near permanent dominance of the vital oil channel.",
