      "title": "Iran’s president denies threatening to resign during talks over strait of Hormuz",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/04/irans-president-denies-threatening-to-resign-during-talks-over-strait-of-hormuz",
      "description": "<p>Masoud Pezeshkian dismisses talk of internal rift as hardline Assembly of Experts call US negotiations ‘futile’</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/aug/04/middle-east-crisis-qatar-iran-us-israel-war-donald-trump-strait-hormuz-gaza-latest-news-updates\">Middle East crisis live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Masoud Pezeshkian, Iran’s president, has been forced to deny claims that he has repeatedly threatened to resign as he battles hardline factions opposed to reaching a settlement with the US over the strait of Hormuz.</p><p>The US and Europe hope a deal is imminent to reopen the strait and they are putting pressure on Oman to accept a temporary agreement that officials in Muscat fear will leave Iran retaining near permanent dominance of the vital oil shipping channel. Ships would enter the strait in a route close to Iran, but leave on a route that passes through Iranian and Omani waters.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/04/irans-president-denies-threatening-to-resign-during-talks-over-strait-of-hormuz\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-04T18:24:35"
    },
    {
      "title": "US and Qatar report progress on Iran ceasefire and reopening Hormuz strait",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/04/us-qatar-progress-iran-ceasefire-hormuz-strait",
      "description": "<p>Optimism echoes Trump’s claims on Monday that deal is close as mediators say they are exchanging proposals </p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/aug/04/middle-east-crisis-qatar-iran-us-israel-war-donald-trump-strait-hormuz-gaza-latest-news-updates\">Middle East crisis live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>US and Qatari officials have said progress is being made in restoring a ceasefire in the US-Iran war and reopening the strait of Hormuz.</p><p>The optimistic speculation on Tuesday brought oil prices down 2%, but the strait remained closed to shipping and a cargo vessel was reportedly struck by an unidentified projectile off Oman’s coast close to the strait.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/04/us-qatar-progress-iran-ceasefire-hormuz-strait\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-04T17:19:58"
    }
